# DROP A WHOLE 2D SPRITE PACK IN HERE.
#
# Sprite bundles ship the same art several times over: individual PNGs, a packed
# atlas, an SVG source set, vector .ai/.eps originals, preview sheets and print
# resolution copies. The ingest reads the raster art and the atlas descriptors;
# the vector sources are usually larger than everything else combined and no
# browser game loads them.
#
# Excluded from the Vercel deploy by .vercelignore, so size here costs git
# history only — but git history is PERMANENT, so it still costs.

# ignore everything...
*

# ...but descend into directories
!*/

# ...and keep the art itself
!*.png
!*.jpg
!*.jpeg
!*.svg

# atlas descriptors — a spritesheet without its .xml/.json is one big image
# nobody can cut up
!*.xml
!*.json
!*.fnt

# licences
!LICENSE*
!License*
!license*
!*.txt

!README.md
!.gitignore
